      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we need to first find out her walking rate in miles per minute. Given that it takes her 24 minutes to walk one mile, her rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Rate} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nNext, to find out how far she will walk in 10 minutes, we multiply her rate by 10 minutes:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the rate (miles per minute)\nrate_miles_per_minute = 1 / 24  # Jana takes 24 minutes to walk one mile\n\n# Calculate the distance for 10 minutes\ntime_minutes = 10\ndistance_miles = rate_miles_per_minute * time_minutes\n\n# Round the result to the nearest tenth\ndistance_miles_rounded = round(distance_miles, 1)\nprint(distance_miles_rounded)\n```\n```output\n0.4\n```\nAfter calculating and rounding, we determine that Jana will walk \\(\\boxed{0.4}\\) miles in 10 minutes.",
