      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we need to determine her walking rate in miles per minute and then apply that rate to the given time. \n\n1. **Determine the rate in miles per minute:** We are given that Jana walks one mile in 24 minutes. So, her walking rate is 1 mile per 24 minutes. \n   \n2. **Calculate the distance in 10 minutes:** We need to find out how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes. To do this, we divide 10 minutes by her walking rate (1 mile per 24 minutes), which gives us \\( \\frac{10}{24} \\) miles per minute.\n   \n3. **Calculate the result:** We multiply the rate by the time to find the distance. So, \\( \\frac{10}{24} \\times 10 = \\frac{100}{24} \\). \n\nNow, let's simplify this fraction and then convert it to a decimal:\n\n\\[ \\frac{100}{24} = \\frac{100 \\div 4}{24 \\div 4} = \\frac{25}{6} \\]\n\nConverting this to a decimal and rounding to the nearest tenth:\n\n\\[ \\frac{25}{6} \\approx 4.167 \\]\n\nRounding 4.167 to the nearest tenth gives us 4.2 miles. Therefore, Jana will walk approximately 4.2 miles in 10 minutes.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{4.2}\\).",
